census for batch 35 -- the cut route; spans 6 .. 12

===== 1. the commissioned CutData is empty =====
  Every contiguous subchain [lo,hi] of bing 0 n of span >= 3 is taken as an
  ambient, with L,H its own band; a runs over its bottom indices and b over
  the later top indices; r over (a,b) with rho r >= H-1 (atR) and r' over
  (r,b) with rho r' <= L+1 (atR').  Counted: those quadruples, and how many
  of them satisfy bandA (rho <= H-2 on [a,r]) and bandB (rho >= L+2 on
  [r,r']).
  span  6 (71 links): 2046 ambients, 66258 crossing quadruples; with bandA 0; with bandB 0; CutData 0
  span  7 (170 links): 13283 ambients, 654535 crossing quadruples; with bandA 0; with bandB 0; CutData 0
  span  8 (409 links): 80801 ambients, 5705345 crossing quadruples; with bandA 0; with bandB 0; CutData 0
  (the clash is local: at r, atR asks for >= H-1 and bandA for <= H-2;
   at r', atR' asks for <= L+1 and bandB for >= L+2.  Hence `not_cutData`.)

===== 2. the corrected cut CutData' =====
  Every contiguous subchain [lo,hi] of span >= 3 is an ambient with its own
  band [L,H]; a is a bottom index of it and b a later top index; r is the
  first index after a at level >= H-2 and r' the first after r at level
  <= L+1.  Measured: whether the level at r is exactly H-2 (the corrected
  atR) and at r' at most L+1, whether the order a < r < r' < b holds, and
  whether the two stretches are strictly inside [L,H] at both ends.
  span  6 (71 links): 1782 cuts; rho r = H-2 in 1782, >= H-1 in 0; rho r' <= L+1 in 1782; order wrong in 0
            [a,r]  above L: 0   below H: 1782   both: 0   (a,r] above L: 1737
            [r,r'] above L: 1735   below H: 1782   both: 1735   (r,r') below H: 1782
  span  7 (170 links): 11366 cuts; rho r = H-2 in 11366, >= H-1 in 0; rho r' <= L+1 in 11366; order wrong in 0
            [a,r]  above L: 0   below H: 11366   both: 0   (a,r] above L: 10947
            [r,r'] above L: 11261   below H: 11366   both: 11261   (r,r') below H: 11366
  span  8 (409 links): 68593 cuts; rho r = H-2 in 68593, >= H-1 in 0; rho r' <= L+1 in 68593; order wrong in 0
            [a,r]  above L: 0   below H: 68593   both: 0   (a,r] above L: 65837
            [r,r'] above L: 68360   below H: 68593   both: 68360   (r,r') below H: 68593
  span  9 (986 links): 405411 cuts; rho r = H-2 in 405411, >= H-1 in 0; rho r' <= L+1 in 405411; order wrong in 0
            [a,r]  above L: 0   below H: 405411   both: 0   (a,r] above L: 388626
            [r,r'] above L: 404881   below H: 405411   both: 404881   (r,r') below H: 405411
  span 10 (2379 links): 2376400 cuts; rho r = H-2 in 2376400, >= H-1 in 0; rho r' <= L+1 in 2376400; order wrong in 0
            [a,r]  above L: 0   below H: 2376400   both: 0   (a,r] above L: 2276991
            [r,r'] above L: 2375165   below H: 2376400   both: 2375165   (r,r') below H: 2376400
  [a,r] contains a, whose level is L exactly, so its band is never strictly
  inside [L,H]; the append lemma does not apply to it
  (`cut_stretchA_no_extension`).

===== 3. the gate: a walk built from the cut, at every interior basepoint =====
  a = last bottom index at or before i, b = first top index at or after i;
  r, r' the first crossings; S the stretch of the cut containing i; C the
  core of S (maximal subinterval containing i avoiding the levels L and H).
  existence: some member of C's free family folds both C-arms at i.
  SOME / EVERY: some / every such member's extension by the two outer legs
  folds both whole arms at i (EVERY also demands the oriented extension be
  a member of the free family of [L,H]).

